== Chapter XIII

#block(inset: (x: 1em))[
  #set par(justify: false)
  #text(size: 0.9em)[#emph[The Ninth Direction. When the heart is disquieted by Sin, speak no peace to it, until God speak it. Peace without detestation of Sin, unsound; So is Peace measured out unto ourselves. How we may know when we measure our peace unto ourselves. Directions as to that Inquiry. The vanity of speaking peace slightly. Also of doing it on one singular account, not universally.]]
]

==== Ninth Direction: Speak No Peace Until God Speaks It

#smallcaps[IN] case God disquiet the Heart about the #emph[Guilt] of its #emph[Distempers] either in respect of its Root and #emph[indwelling,] or in respect of any Eruptions of it, take heed thou #emph[speakest not peace to thyself before God speaks it; but hearken what he says to thy Soul:] This is our next Direction, without the Observation whereof, the Heart will be exceedingly exposed to the #emph[deceitfulness] of Sin.

This is a business of great importance. It is a sad thing for a man to deceive his own Soul herein. All the warnings God gives us in tenderness to our Souls, to try and examine ourselves, do tend to the preventing of this great Evil of speaking #emph[peace groundlessly] to #emph[ourselves,] which is upon the issue to bless ourselves in an opposition to God. It is not my business to insist upon the danger of it, but to help Believers to prevent it, and to let them know when they do so.

To manage this Direction aright, observe,

(1) That as it is the great #emph[Prerogative] and #emph[Sovereignty] of God to give grace to whom he pleases, (#emph[he hath mercy on whom he will,] Rom 9:18 and among all the #emph[Sons] of men, He #emph[calls whom he will,] and sanctifies whom he #emph[will,]) so among those so #emph[called] and #emph[justified,] and whom he will save, He yet reserves this Privilege to himself, to speak Peace to whom he pleaseth, and in what Degree he pleaseth, even amongst them on whom he hath bestowed #emph[Grace.] He is the God of #emph[all Consolation,] in an especial manner in his dealing with Believers: That is, of the #emph[good things] that he keeps locked up in his Family, and gives out of it to all his Children at his pleasure. This the Lord insists on, Isa 57:16, 17, 18. It is the case under Consideration that is there insisted on. When God says he will #emph[heal] their Breaches and Disconsolations, he assumes this Privilege to himself in an especial manner. #emph[I create it,] v. 19. Even in respect of these poor wounded Creatures, #emph[I create it,] and according to my sovereignty make it out as I please.

Hence as it is with the #emph[collation of Grace] in reference to them that are in the state of Nature; God doth it in great Curiosity, and his proceedings therein, in taking and leaving, as to outward Appearances, quite besides, and contrary oft-times to all probable Expectations; so is it in his #emph[Communication of Peace] and Joy in reference unto them that are in the state of Grace; he gives them out oft times quite besides our expectation, as to any appearing Grounds of his Dispensations.

(2) As #emph[God creates] it for whom he #emph[pleaseth,] so it is the Prerogative of Christ, to speak it #emph[home] to the Conscience: Speaking to the Church of #emph[Laodicea,] who had healed her wounds #emph[falsely,] and spoke #emph[peace] to her #emph[self] when she #emph[ought] not, He takes to himself that #emph[Title, I am the Amen]\; the #emph[faithful witness,] Rev 3:14. He bears #emph[testimony] concerning our Condition as it is indeed; we may possibly mistake, and trouble ourselves in vain, or flatter ourselves upon false Grounds, but he is the #emph[Amen,] the faithful #emph[witness,] and what he speaks of our State and Condition, that it is indeed, Isa 11:3. He is said not to #emph[judge according to the sight of the eye,] not according to any outward appearance, or any thing that may be subject to a mistake, as we are apt to do; but He shall judge and #emph[determine] every #emph[cause] as it is indeed.

Take these two previous Observations, and I shall give some #emph[Rules] whereby men may know whether God #emph[speaks peace] to them, or whether they speak #emph[peace] to themselves only.

(1) Men certainly #emph[speak peace to themselves,] when their so doing is not #emph[attended] with the greatest #emph[detestation] imaginable of that #emph[sin] in reference whereunto they do speak Peace to themselves, and #emph[abhorrency] of themselves for it. When men are #emph[wounded] by sin, #emph[disquieted] and #emph[perplexed,] and knowing that there is no #emph[remedy] for them, but only in the #emph[mercies] of God through the #emph[blood of Christ,] do therefore #emph[look] to him, and to the #emph[Promises] of the Covenant in him, and thereupon quiet their #emph[hearts] that it shall be well with them, and that God will be exalted that he may be gracious to them, and yet their Souls are not #emph[wrought] to the #emph[greatest] detestation of the sin or sins upon the Account whereof they are disquieted; this is to heal themselves, and not to be healed of #emph[God.] This is but a #emph[great] and #emph[strong wind,] that the Lord is #emph[nigh] unto, but the Lord is not in the wind. When men do truly look upon Christ whom they have #emph[pierced,] (without which there is no Healing or Peace,) they will #emph[mourn,] Zech 12:10 they will #emph[mourn for him] even upon this account, and detest the #emph[sin] that pierced him. When we go to Christ for #emph[healing,] Faith eyes him #emph[peculiarly] as one #emph[pierced.] Faith takes several #emph[views] of Christ according to the #emph[Occasions] of Address to him, and #emph[communion] with him that it hath. Sometimes it views his #emph[Holiness,] sometimes his #emph[power,] sometimes his #emph[love,] his #emph[favor] with his Father. And when it goes for #emph[healing] and #emph[peace,] it looks especially on the #emph[blood] of the Covenant, on his Sufferings; for by his #emph[stripes are we healed,] and #emph[the chastisement of our peace was upon him,] Isa 53:5 when we look for Healing, his #emph[stripes] are to be eyed; not in the outward story of them, which is the course of #emph[Popish Devotionists,] but in the #emph[Love, Kindness, Mystery] and design of the Cross. And when we look for #emph[peace,] his #emph[Chastisements] must be in our eye: Now this I say, if it be #emph[done] according to the #emph[mind] of God, and in the #emph[strength] of that #emph[Spirit] which is poured out on Believers, it will beget a detestation of that sin or sins, for which #emph[healing] and #emph[peace] is sought. So Ezek 16:60, 61. Nevertheless #emph[I will remember my Covenant with thee in the days of thy youth, and I will establish unto thee an everlasting Covenant,] and what then? #emph[then thou shalt remember thy ways and be ashamed.] When God comes home to speak #emph[peace] in a #emph[sure Covenant] of it, it fills the Soul with #emph[shame] for all the #emph[ways] whereby it hath been alienated from him. And one of the things that the Apostle mentions as attending that #emph[godly sorrow] which is accompanied with #emph[Repentance] unto Salvation never to be repented of, is #emph[revenge, yea what revenge,] 2 Cor 7:11. They reflected on their #emph[miscarriages] with #emph[Indignation] and Revenge for their Folly in them. When #emph[Job] comes up to a thorough #emph[healing,] he cries, #emph[Now I abhor myself,] Job 42:6 and until he did so, he had no #emph[abiding peace.] He might perhaps have #emph[made up himself] with that Doctrine of #emph[free Grace] which was so excellently #emph[preached] by #emph[Elihu]\; ch. 33 from v. 14 unto the 29th, but he had then but #emph[skinned] his wounds, he must come to #emph[self-abhorrency,] if he come to healing. So was it with those in Psalm 78:33, 35 in their #emph[great trouble and perplexity] for and upon the Account of Sin; I doubt not but upon the Address they made to God in Christ, (for that so they did, is evident from the titles they gave him, they call him their #emph[Rock] and their #emph[Redeemer,] two words every where pointing out the Lord Christ) they spake peace to themselves; but was it #emph[sound] and #emph[abiding]? No, it passed away as the #emph[early dew:] God speaks not one word of peace to their Souls. But why had they not peace? Why, because in their #emph[Address] to God they #emph[flattered him:] But how doth that appear? v. 37. #emph[Their heart was not right with him, neither were they steadfast.] They had not a #emph[detestation] nor #emph[relinquishment] of that sin, in reference whereunto they #emph[spake peace] to themselves: Let a man make what #emph[application] he will for #emph[healing] and #emph[peace,] let him do it to the true #emph[Physician,] let him do it the #emph[right way,] let him quiet his Heart in the Promises of the Covenant; yet when Peace is #emph[spoken,] if it be not #emph[attended] with the detestation and Abhorrency of that Sin which was the #emph[wound,] and caused the Disquietment, this is no Peace of Gods #emph[creating,] but of our own #emph[purchasing.] It is but a #emph[skinning] over the #emph[wound,] whilst the #emph[core] lies at the bottom, which will #emph[putrefy] and #emph[corrupt,] and corrode, until it break out again with #emph[noisomeness,] vexation and danger. Let not poor Souls that #emph[walk] in such a path as this, (they are more #emph[sensible] of the #emph[trouble] of Sin, than of the #emph[pollution] or uncleanness that attends it; they #emph[address] themselves for #emph[mercy,] yea to the Lord in Christ they address themselves for #emph[mercy,] but yet will keep the sweet Morsel of their Sin under their Tongue,) let them (I say) never think to have #emph[true] and #emph[solid] peace. For instance, Thou findest thy Heart running out after the World, and it disturbs thee in thy #emph[communion] with God; the Spirit speaks expressly to thee, #emph[He that loveth the World, the love of the Father is not in him,] 1 John 2:15. This puts #emph[thee] on dealing with God in Christ for the #emph[healing] of thy Soul, the #emph[quieting] of thy Conscience; but yet withal a thorough #emph[detestation] of the #emph[evil] itself abides not upon thee; yea perhaps that is liked well enough, but only in respect of the #emph[Consequences] of it; perhaps thou mayst be saved, yet as through #emph[fire]\; and God will have some work with thee before he hath done, but thou wilt have little Peace in this Life; thou wilt be #emph[sick] and fainting all thy days, Isa 57:17. This is a Deceit that lies at the #emph[root] of the Peace of many Professors, and wastes it; they deal with all their strength about Mercy and Pardon; and seem to have great #emph[Communion] with God in their so doing: they lie before him, #emph[bewail] their Sins and Follies, that any one would think (yea they think themselves) that surely they and their Sins are now parted, and so receive in Mercy that #emph[satisfies] their Hearts for a little season; but when a thorough search comes to be made, there hath been some secret #emph[reserve] for the Folly or Follies treated about; at least there hath not been that thorough Abhorrency of it which is necessary; and their whole #emph[peace] is quickly discovered to be weak and rotten; scarce abiding any longer than the words of begging it are in their mouths.

(2) When men measure out #emph[peace] to themselves upon the #emph[conclusions] that their #emph[convictions] and Rational Principles will carry them out unto; This is a false peace, and will not abide. I shall a little explain what I mean hereby. A man hath got a wound by sin, he hath a Conviction of some Sin upon his Conscience, he hath not #emph[walked] uprightly as becometh the Gospel; all is not well and right between God and his Soul: He considers now what is to be done; Light he hath, and knows what Path he must take, and how his Soul hath been formerly healed. Considering that the #emph[Promises] of God are the outward Means of Application for the #emph[healing] of his sores, and quieting of his Heart, he goes to them, #emph[searches] them out, #emph[finds] out some one or #emph[more] of them, whose #emph[literal] Expressions are directly suited to his #emph[condition:] Says he to himself, God speaks in this Promise, here I will take my #emph[self] a plaster as long and broad as my #emph[wound,] and so brings the word of the #emph[promise] to his #emph[Condition,] and sets him down in peace. This is another #emph[appearance] upon the #emph[mount,] the Lord is near, but the Lord is not in it. It hath not been the work of the Spirit, (who alone can convince us of #emph[Sin] and #emph[Righteousness] and #emph[Judgment,])#footnote[John 16:8.] but the mere Actings of the intelligent rational Soul. As there are three sorts of Lives (we say,) the #emph[vegetative,] the #emph[sensitive] and the #emph[rational] or intelligent. Some #emph[things] have only the #emph[vegetative]\; some the #emph[sensitive] also, and that includes the former; some have the #emph[rational,] which takes #emph[in] and supposes both the other. Now he that hath the #emph[rational,] he doth not only act suitably to that #emph[principle,] but also to #emph[both] the others, he grows and is sensible. It is so with men in the things of God; some are mere #emph[natural] and #emph[rational] men; some have a #emph[superadded] Conviction with #emph[Illumination]\; and some are truly #emph[regenerate.] Now he that hath the #emph[latter,] hath also both the #emph[former]\; and therefore he acts sometimes upon the Principles of the #emph[rational,] sometimes upon the Principles of the #emph[enlightened man.] His true #emph[spiritual life] is not the #emph[principle] of all his #emph[motions]\; He acts not always in the #emph[strength] thereof, neither are all his #emph[fruits] from that Root. In this case that I speak of, he acts merely upon the Principle of #emph[Conviction] and Illumination, whereby his first #emph[naturals] are heightened; but the Spirit breathes not at all upon all these #emph[waters.] Take an Instance; suppose the wound and disquiet of the Soul to be upon the account of Relapses, which whatever the #emph[evil] or Folly be, though for the matter of it, never so #emph[small,] yet there are no wounds deeper than those that are given the Soul on that account, nor disquietments greater. In the perturbation of his Mind, he finds out that Promise, Isa 55:7. #emph[The Lord will have mercy, and our God will abundantly pardon]\; He will multiply or add to pardon; He will do it again and #emph[again]\; or that in Hosea 14:4. #emph[I will heal their backsliding, I will love them freely]\; This the man considers, and thereupon concludes Peace to himself; whether the #emph[Spirit] of God make the Application or no, whether that gives #emph[life] and #emph[power] to the #emph[letter] or no, that he #emph[regards] not. He doth not hearken whether God #emph[the Lord speak peace.] He doth not wait upon God, who perhaps yet #emph[hides his face,] and sees the poor Creature #emph[stealing] Peace and running away with it, knowing that the time #emph[will] come when he will deal with him again, and call him to a new #emph[reckoning]\; Hos 9:9 when he shall see that it is in vain to go one step where God doth not take him by the hand.

I see here indeed sundry other #emph[questions] upon this arising and interposing themselves: I cannot apply myself to them all: one I shall a little speak to.

It may be said then, #emph[seeing] that this seems to be the path that the Holy Spirit leads us in, for the healing of our #emph[wounds,] and quieting of our #emph[hearts,] how shall we know when we go alone ourselves, and when the #emph[Spirit] also doth accompany us?

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[#emph[Ans.] 1. If any of you are out of the way upon this account, God will speedily let you know it; for besides that you have his Promise, that #emph[the meek he will guide in judgment, and teach them his way,] Ps 25:9 he will not let you always err. He will (I say) not suffer your #emph[nakedness] to be covered with #emph[Fig-leaves,] but take them #emph[away,] and all the peace you have in them, and will not suffer you to #emph[settle] on such #emph[lees]\; you shall quickly #emph[know] your #emph[wound] is not healed. That is, you shall speedily know whether or no it be thus with you by the #emph[event]\; the peace you thus get and obtain, will not abide. Whilst the Mind is overpowered by its own Convictions, there is no hold for disquietments to fix upon. Stay a little and all these reasonings will grow cold, and vanish before the face of the first Temptation that arises. But,]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. This course is commonly taken without #emph[waiting]\; which is the Grace, and that peculiar acting of #emph[Faith] which God #emph[calls] for to be exercised in such a Condition. I know God doth sometimes come in upon the Soul instantly, in a #emph[moment] as it were, wounding and healing it; as I am persuaded it was in the Case of #emph[David] when he cut off the #emph[lap] of #emph[Saul's] Garment: But #emph[ordinarily] in such a case God calls for #emph[waiting] and #emph[laboring,] #footnote[Ps 123:2. Ps 130:6.] attending as the eye of a Servant upon his Master: Says the Prophet #emph[Isaiah,] ch. 8:17. #emph[I will wait upon the Lord, who hideth his face from Jacob.] God will have his #emph[Children] lie a while at his door, when they have #emph[run] from his House, and not instantly #emph[rush] in upon him; unless he take them by the #emph[hand,] and pluck them in, when they are so ashamed that they #emph[dare] not come to him. Now #emph[self-healers,] or men that speak peace to themselves, do commonly make #emph[haste,] they will not tarry; They do not #emph[hearken] what God speaks, Isa 28:16 but on they will go to be healed.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[3\. Such a Course, though it may quiet the #emph[Conscience] and the #emph[Mind,] the rational concluding part of the Soul, yet it doth not #emph[sweeten] the Heart with Rest and gracious Contentation. The Answer it receives is much like that #emph[Elisha] gave #emph[Naaman, Go in peace]\; 2 Kgs 5:19 it quieted his Mind, but I much question whether it #emph[sweetened] his Heart, or gave him any #emph[Joy in Believing,] other than the #emph[natural] Joy that was then #emph[stirred] in him upon his healing. #emph[Do not my words do good,] saith the Lord, Mic 2:7. When God speaks, there is not only #emph[truth] in his words, that may answer the #emph[Conviction] of our Understanding, but also they do good, they bring #emph[that] which is #emph[sweet] and #emph[good] and #emph[desirable] to the Will and Affections: By them the Soul returns unto its Rest, Ps 116:7.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[4\. Which is worst of all, it #emph[amends] not the #emph[life,] it heals not the #emph[evil,] it cures not the #emph[distemper]: When God speaks Peace, it guides and #emph[keeps] the Soul that it turn not again to Folly, Ps 85:8. When we speak it ourselves, the Heart is not taken off the Evil. Nay it is the readiest course in the world to bring a Soul into a trade of Backsliding. If upon thy #emph[plastering] thyself, thou findest thyself rather animated to the #emph[battle] again, than utterly #emph[weaned] from it, it is too #emph[palpable] that thou hast been at #emph[work] with thy own Soul, but Jesus Christ and his Spirit were not there. Yea and often-times #emph[Nature] having done its work, will ere a few days are over come for its Reward; and having been #emph[active] in the work of Healing, will be ready to reason for a new wounding. In Gods speaking peace there comes along so much #emph[sweetness] and such a Discovery of his #emph[Love,] #footnote[Luke 22:32.] as is a strong Obligation on the Soul no more to deal perversely.]]

#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[(3) We #emph[speak Peace] to ourselves, when we do it #emph[slightly.] This the Prophet complains of in some Teachers, Jer 6:14. #emph[They have healed the wound of the Daughter of my people slightly.] And it is so with #emph[some persons,] they make the healing of their #emph[wounds] a slight work, a #emph[look,] a #emph[glance] of Faith to the #emph[Promises] does it, and so the matter is ended. The Apostle tells us, that the Word did not profit some, because it was not #emph[mixed with Faith,] Heb 4:2 μὴ συγκεκραμένος, it was not well tempered and mingled with Faith. It is not a mere #emph[look] to the word of Mercy in the Promise, but it must be #emph[mingled] with Faith until it is #emph[incorporated] into the very Nature of it; and then indeed it doth good unto the Soul: If thou hast had a wound upon thy Conscience, which was attended with #emph[weakness] and #emph[disquietness,] which now thou art #emph[freed] of, How camest thou so? I looked to the Promises of #emph[pardon] and #emph[healing,] and so found Peace: Yea but perhaps thou hast made too much haste, thou hast done it overly, thou hast not fed upon the Promise, so as to mix it with Faith, to have got all the #emph[virtue] of it #emph[diffused] into thy Soul; only thou hast done it #emph[slightly]\; thou wilt find thy wound #emph[ere] it be long breaking out again, and thou shalt know that thou art not cured.]

(4) Whoever speaks #emph[peace] to himself upon any one account, and at the same time hath another Evil of no less #emph[importance] lying upon his Spirit, about which he #emph[hath] had no dealing with God, that man cries #emph[Peace] when there is none. A little to explain my Meaning: A man hath neglected a Duty again and again, perhaps when in all #emph[Righteousness] it was due from him; his Conscience is perplexed, his Soul wounded, he hath no quiet in his Bones by reason of his Sin; he applies himself for Healing, and finds Peace. Yet in the mean time perhaps #emph[worldliness,] or Pride, or some other #emph[folly] wherewith the Spirit of God is exceedingly #emph[grieved,] may lie in the bosom of that man, and they neither disturb him, nor he them. Let not that man think that any of his Peace is from God.

Then shall it be well with men when they have an equal respect to #emph[all] Gods Commandments. God will #emph[justify] us #emph[from] our #emph[sins,] but he will not justify the least sin in us; He is a God of #emph[purer] eyes than to behold Iniquity.

(5) When men of themselves #emph[speak peace] to their Consciences, it is seldom that God speaks #emph[humiliation] to their Souls: Gods Peace is #emph[humbling] Peace, #emph[melting] Peace, as it was in the case of #emph[David]\; Ps 51:1. Never such deep #emph[humiliation] as when #emph[Nathan] brought him the tidings of his Pardon.

#emph[Q.] But you will say, #emph[When may we take the comfort of a] Promise #emph[as our own, in relation to some peculiar wound for the quieting the Heart.]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[#emph[A.] 1. In general, when God #emph[speaks] it, be it when it will, sooner or later. I told you before, He may do it in the #emph[very] instant of the sin itself, and that with such #emph[irresistible power,] that the Soul must needs receive his #emph[mind] in it. Sometimes he will make us #emph[wait] longer; but when he speaks, be it sooner or later, be it when we are sinning or repenting, be the Condition of our Souls what they please, if God #emph[speak] he must be received. There is not any thing that in our Communion with him the Lord is more troubled with us for, (if I may so say) than our #emph[unbelieving] Fears that keep us off from receiving that strong #emph[consolation] which he is so willing to give to us.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[But you will say, #emph[We are where we were; when God speaks it, we must receive it; that is true, but how shall we know when he] speaks?]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[#emph[Ans.] 1. I would we could all #emph[practically] come up to this, to receive #emph[peace] when we are convinced that God speaks it, and that it is our Duty to receive it; But,]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. There is (if I may so say) a secret instinct in Faith, whereby it knows the voice of Christ, when He speaks indeed; as the #emph[babe] leaped in the #emph[womb] when the blessed #emph[Virgin] came to #emph[Elizabeth]\; Faith leaps in the #emph[heart] when Christ indeed #emph[draws] nigh to it; #emph[My sheep] (says Christ) #emph[know my voice,] John 10:4, they #emph[know my voice,] they are used to the sound of it, and they know when his lips are opened to them, and are full of Grace: The #emph[spouse] was in a sad condition, Song 5:2. #emph[asleep in security]\; but yet as soon as Christ speaks she cries, it is #emph[the voice of my beloved that speaks]\; She knew his voice, and was so #emph[acquainted] with communion with him that instantly she discovers him: and so will you also: if you exercise yourselves to acquaintance and #emph[communion] with him, you will easily discern between his #emph[voice] and the voice of a stranger. And take this κριτήριον with you; when he doth speak he speaks as never man spake; He speaks with power, and one way or other will make your hearts burn within you, as He did to the #emph[Disciples,] Luke 24. He doth it by putting in his hand at the hole of the #emph[door,] Song 5:4 his spirit into your #emph[hearts to seize on you.]]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[He that hath his #emph[senses exercised to discern] good or evil, being increased in judgment and experience, by a constant observation of the ways of Christ's #emph[intercourse,] the manner of the operations of the spirit, and the effects it usually produceth, is the best judge for himself in this case.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. If the word of the Lord doth good to your souls, He speaks it. If it humble, if it #emph[cleanse] and be useful for those ends, for which #emph[promises] are given: #emph[viz.] 1. To #emph[endear,] 2. #emph[cleanse,] 3\. To #emph[Melt] and bind to Obedience, 4. To #emph[self-emptiness,] etc. But this is not my business: Nor shall I farther #emph[divert] in the pursuit of this #emph[Direction]\; without the observation of it, Sin will have great Advantages towards the hardening of the Heart.]]
